# CODEOWNERS — maker / checker / signer segregation-of-duties (plan 083)
#
# Purpose: enforce four-eyes (two-person) review on the publish path. The
# release flow is the changesets two-phase flow (`.changeset/config.json`
# `"commit": false`, `"baseBranch": "main"`):
#
#   maker   — opens a PR carrying a changeset and/or the auto-generated
#             Version PR that bumps `packages/*/package.json` versions and
#             changelogs. (The author of the change.)
#   checker — a DISTINCT reviewer (NOT the maker) who must approve the PR.
#             GitHub enforces this when "Require review from Code Owners" is
#             enabled on the `main` branch protection rule: a PR that edits
#             any path below CANNOT merge without a code-owner approval, and
#             GitHub will not count the PR author's own review. This is the
#             second person of the four-eyes control.
#   signer  — the `Release` workflow's publish step (`release.yml`), which is
#             additionally gated behind the protected GitHub `release-signing`
#             Environment. The signer step only runs after the environment's
#             required-reviewer gate releases `NPM_TOKEN` (see release.yml).
#
# This is a CI/ops control, NOT a kernel control: it never runs inside
# `adjudicate()` and changes no package source. It can only ADD friction to
# the merge/publish path (more required reviewers), never authorize a release
# the existing gates would refuse (§C monotonicity; §D constitutional
# invariant #6 fail-closed — a missing checker approval blocks the merge, so
# publish never happens by default).
#
# NOTE: the handles below are placeholders for the project's maintainer
# group. Replace `@adjudicate/maintainers` (and, for the most sensitive
# version-bump surface, the distinct `@adjudicate/release-checkers`) with the
# real GitHub team slugs before relying on CODEOWNERS enforcement. The teams
# MUST be disjoint from the set of routine change authors for the four-eyes
# property to hold.

# ── Default ownership: every change gets a maintainer review. ───────────────
*                               @adjudicate/maintainers

# ── Publish-path surface: the maker's version-bump artifacts. ───────────────
# A changeset declares the intended release; the auto-generated Version PR
# rewrites these package manifests. A DISTINCT checker (the release-checkers
# team — disjoint from the maker) must approve any edit here. This is the
# four-eyes gate over what actually gets published.
/.changeset/**                  @adjudicate/release-checkers
/packages/*/package.json        @adjudicate/release-checkers

# ── Release/CI machinery: the segregation controls themselves. ──────────────
# Edits to the publish workflow, the CODEOWNERS policy, or the kernel-purity /
# release gates must themselves go through code-owner review so the
# maker/checker/signer separation cannot be silently weakened.
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @adjudicate/release-checkers
/.github/workflows/release.yml  @adjudicate/release-checkers
/.github/workflows/ci.yml       @adjudicate/maintainers
/.github/workflows/release-candidate.yml @adjudicate/maintainers
/scripts/rc-checks.ts           @adjudicate/maintainers
/scripts/check-freeze-matrix.ts @adjudicate/maintainers
